# Global build discipline (builder)

**Mandatory read:** [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) — GrantPilot Engine Constitution (distilled). Do not duplicate constitution text here.

## Builder charter

Builds from versioned package specs only, scoped to the spec. Plan-first; AMBER plans halt for owner approval. Runs /review before every push. Never certifies, never audits, never edits goldens, the constitution, or hook configs. When the spec and observed behaviour disagree, stops and reports — the spec is amended, not the chat.

## Spec locations and contract hygiene

- Contract docs in `docs/artefacts/` and `docs/artefacts/me_module/` are truth; code obeys them.
- Do not retroactively change contracts to match code without a decision-log entry and explicit approval.
- M&E contracts lock in Stage B; no M&E product code before Stage B exit.

## Diagnose before fixing

Diagnose before fixing — structured root-cause before any patch.

## Backend is source of truth

- All reasoning, entitlements, gates, and AI live server-side.
- Frontend (separate repo) renders and calls the API only; adapt UI to contract, never reverse.

## Scope drift

If a prompt drifts into M&E non-goals (field collection, dashboards, logframe live system, Level-3 autonomy, modifying core proposal/export services), **STOP** and flag — do not implement.

## Decision log

- Locked or revised choices go in `docs/artefacts/me_module/ME_MODULE_DECISION_LOG.md`.
- Append; do not silently pivot. Reference the log when resolving ambiguity.
